# Git for Windows checks out with `core.autocrlf=true` by default, which rewrites LF to CRLF
# on the way into the working tree. Without this file that is wrong twice over:
#
#   * The fixture trees stand in for real mod files, and the installer copies those byte for
#     byte. A converted fixture makes the Windows tests exercise different bytes from the
#     Linux ones - silently, until an assertion compares file contents and reads back a
#     `\r\n` that was never committed.
#   * The fonts, icons and snapshot baselines are binary. Any conversion corrupts them.
#
# Everything is stored as LF and checked out as LF, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures are stand-ins for files copied verbatim, so nothing may be rewritten in either
# direction - not on checkout, and not on commit either.
crates/core/tests/fixtures/** -text

# Binary by extension, listed rather than left to Git's guess: a misdetected font or a
# misdetected PNG is a corrupt file, and the failure appears far from the cause.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.dll binary
